# A seeded Frobenius class has positive prime density (clean spine)

Theorem statement: `HorizontalPadicL.seededFrobeniusClass_positiveDensity_v2`
(`1e0efce4-1fe8-4c9b-802d-94a3674fd74d`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25.

Proof: submission `b9265b5d-2718-4daa-a574-62a007bbb4c9`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

The set of rational primes represented by the seeded Frobenius conjugacy class, after deletion of
finitely many excluded primes, has positive natural density relative to the primes. Its density is
the size of the conjugacy class divided by the order of the finite Galois group.

This is a clean-spine replacement used to remove deprecated definition bundles from the live graph.

## Explanation of the source proof

Unpack the seeded Chebotarev-class realization as a finite Galois extension, a conjugacy class
representative, and a finite excluded set. Chebotarev gives natural density equal to the size of the
conjugacy class divided by the order of the Galois group. Both cardinalities are positive because
the class contains its representative and the group contains that element. The defining realization
identifies the counted Chebotarev primes with the seeded prime set.

